   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Ruth, you're verified. I found yesterday's ticket for the missing garlic knots on your Big Slice Pizza order (Q-7690). The agent promised you a $6.50 credit, but it was never applied to your account.\n\nI've now added the $6.50 credit. Your account balance is $6.50, and you can use it on a future order. I'm sorry for the delay.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thank you for finding that. I was told it would be a credit, but I thought the amount was $10, not $6.50. I'm not completely sure about the exact number, though, since I don't have the chat from yesterday in front of me. Could you check what was promised on that ticket?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the ticket (TK-881, created yesterday at 8:15 PM). It records a promise of **$6.50** in account credit for the missing garlic knots. That matches the garlic knots' price on your order, which was $6.50.\n\nI can only issue what the ticket records, so $6.50 is the amount I can honor. I've applied it, and your balance is now $6.50.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, if the ticket says $6.50, then I'll accept that. I was fairly sure it was $10, but I don't have the chat in front of me to prove it, so I won't argue the number. Thank you for applying the credit and for checking. That's all I needed today."
  }
